# Cloudflare Pages response headers.
#
# Path prefixes are kept NON-OVERLAPPING on purpose: when two rules match the
# same URL, a duplicated header (Cache-Control in particular) is ambiguous.
#
# /assets/*  Vite's content-hashed bundles. The hash changes whenever the
#            bytes change, so a URL's content is immutable.
# /fonts/*   Version is baked into the filename (…-v2.304-subset.woff2), so
#            the same reasoning applies.
# /static/*  Stable filenames (samples, share card). Week-long TTL with
#            background revalidation.
# Canonical HTML routes are always revalidated, and deliberately do NOT carry
#            no-transform. Cloudflare honours no-transform by disabling response
#            compression (RFC 9111 §5.2.2.6), which cost 70% of HTML transfer —
#            178KB down to 53KB across the 14 routes — on the LCP critical path.
#            Dropping it is only safe because the zone's Web Analytics (RUM)
#            site was DELETED at the same time, 2026-09-01. no-transform had
#            been suppressing the beacon INJECTION, which is not what CSP does:
#            script-src 'self' stops the beacon from loading, but the <script>
#            tag still lands in the markup, which spams the console and makes
#            faq.html's "no analytics script" claim false. Re-creating a RUM
#            site for this zone brings it straight back — see AGENTS.md trap 16.
#            Note Cloudflare only injects when the request looks like a browser
#            (browser User-Agent AND Accept: text/html), so a plain curl check
#            is a false negative.
#            The one edge rewrite CSP would NOT catch is Email Obfuscation:
#            it injects from same-origin /cdn-cgi/ and is on at the zone, but
#            only fires on mailto: links, and there are none in the served HTML.
#            Never put an email address in the markup — link the repo's issue
#            tracker instead. src/seo.test.ts pins that half.
#            Zone state when this was changed: rocket_loader off, mirage off,
#            email_obfuscation on, no RUM site.
# /*         Baseline hardening + a content policy that ENFORCES the privacy
#            claim instead of just asserting it: connect-src 'none' means the
#            page cannot open a fetch/XHR/WebSocket to anywhere, so a dropped
#            image has no route off the device even if the code tried.
#            This also blocks Cloudflare Web Analytics (and any other) beacons
#            on purpose — traffic is observed only as edge HTTP request counts.
#            HSTS upgrades returning visitors before any HTTP request leaves
#            the browser. It deliberately excludes subdomains and preload.

/assets/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

/fonts/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

/static/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=604800, stale-while-revalidate=86400

/
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate

/tool
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate

/usecases
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate

/faq
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate

/privacy
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate

/charsets/standard
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate

/charsets/detailed
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate

/charsets/blocks
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate

/charsets/minimal
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate

/charsets/binary
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate

/charsets/braille
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate

/guides/readme-banner
